Emulator: a hub port reset that enables the port reports C_PORT_RESET alone. USB 2.0 11.24.2.7.2.2 sets
C_PORT_ENABLE only when the port is disabled by a Port_Error; dev-hub.c recorded it on the enable as well, so
AppleUSBHub took every reset port as one the hardware had disabled and enumerated its device again.

diff --git a/hw/usb/dev-hub.c b/hw/usb/dev-hub.c
--- a/hw/usb/dev-hub.c
+++ b/hw/usb/dev-hub.c
@@ -421,7 +421,12 @@
                 usb_hub_port_clear(port, PORT_STAT_RESET);
                 if (pdev && pdev->attached) {
                     usb_device_reset(pdev);
-                    usb_hub_port_set(port, PORT_STAT_ENABLE);
+                    /*
+                     * USB 2.0 11.24.2.7.2.2: C_PORT_ENABLE is set only when a
+                     * port is disabled by a Port_Error. A reset that enables
+                     * the port reports C_PORT_RESET alone.
+                     */
+                    port->wPortStatus |= PORT_STAT_ENABLE;
                 }
                 usb_wakeup(s->intr, 0);
                 break;
